    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to maximize floor stability while keeping an eye on our scarcity targets. **Kyle Tucker** (67.14) remains our premier start, as he faces a favorable matchup despite the uncertainty surrounding the lineup position; his elite power-speed profile makes him a lock against an arm like Robbie Ray. **Gunnar Henderson** (63.38) is our second-strongest play, buoyed significantly by a +16% park factor and favorable wind conditions that help offset the challenge of facing a tough southpaw like Fried. **Sam Antonacci** (60.16) rounds out our top-tier group, as his leadoff spot and excellent xwOBA (0.391) against Lugo provide a high-floor opportunity to accumulate runs and steals, which are vital given our team strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the benching of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.93), who narrowly missed the cut. While his profile is robust, the combination of a difficult matchup against an elite arm and our strict scoring threshold kept him on the pine in favor of players like **Liam Hicks** (59.92) and **Drake Baldwin** (59.56), both of whom benefit from more advantageous SP_xERA matchups. We are closely monitoring the lineup for **Heliot Ramos**, whose score of 42.04 is suppressed by a brutal matchup against Shohei Ohtani; he remains in the lineup only because of his potential to contribute in a category-diverse set, but he is at risk if his batting order slips. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose IL statuses continue to limit our bench flexibility, forcing us to rely on our active depth to maintain offensive output.",
